Build a bilingual (Arabic/English) web app called "SmallSteps" that helps employees make steady progress toward a high-level work objective by always suggesting the next small actionable step, tracking what they did, and preventing repeated suggestions.

IMPORTANT PRODUCT RULES
- The product is ALWAYS individual-only. No Team Mode, no manager dashboards, no shared objectives.
- Later we support exporting a progress report for the user to share with their manager, but still individual-only.

TECH STACK
- Next.js 14+ (App Router) + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- next-intl for i18n (ar/en) with full RTL support for Arabic
- Prisma + PostgreSQL

- Auth: email + password (NO OTP). Use NextAuth credentials provider OR custom auth. Hash passwords with bcrypt.
- Password reset via email link is allowed (for recovery only).
- OpenAI API for step generation (OPENAI_API_KEY). Validate outputs with zod.

BRANDING / UI
- Youthful, modern UI with a vibrant gradient accent (do not use dull corporate colors).
- Clean, minimal but energetic: rounded cards, subtle shadows, lively highlights, smooth micro-interactions.
- Support Dark Mode + Light Mode.
- Arabic: RTL layout. English: LTR. Numeric fields centered; text aligned by locale.
- Add a compact top bar with logo + app name "SmallSteps".
- Add a simple onboarding screen explaining: "Write your objective → get the next step → act → track progress".

LOGO DESIGN (create assets in-code)
- Design a simple, modern vector logo (SVG) that fits the brand:
  - Icon concept: 3 ascending rounded steps forming an upward path, optionally with a small arrow/spark at the top.
  - Style: flat/duotone, works in mono too.
  - Provide 2 variants: full (icon + wordmark) and icon-only.
  - Provide as SVG files in /public/brand:
    - /public/brand/smallsteps-icon.svg
    - /public/brand/smallsteps-full.svg
- Wordmark: “SmallSteps” (English) and “خطوات صغيرة” (Arabic) as optional lockup; ensure legibility at small sizes.

CORE USER FLOW
1) Sign up / login:
   - Sign up: email + password + locale preference (ar/en)
   - Login: email + password + remember me
   - Optional: "Continue as Guest" (stores data locally only)
2) Dashboard:
   - List Objectives (active / archived)
   - Create objective (title + optional description + optional constraints)
3) Objective details:
   - Button: "Generate Next Step"
   - Show a "Step Card" with:
     - step_title (verb + object, very concrete)
     - expected_outcome
     - prerequisites (array)
     - estimated_minutes (10/20/30/45/60)
     - dependency (none / needs-approval / waiting-on-someone)
     - optional template (email/message/checklist)
   - User actions:
     A) "I will do this" -> status planned
     B) "Already done" -> status done
     C) "Regenerate" -> new suggestion that differs materially
     D) "Not applicable" -> status skipped + reason (no access / missing info / depends on others / irrelevant)
   - Progress panel:
     - counts of planned/done/skipped
     - a simple progress indicator + “streak” (days with at least 1 step marked planned/done)

REPORT EXPORT (individual-only)
- Provide an "Export Report" button per objective:
  - Exports a clean report in PDF and Markdown:
    - Objective title + timeframe
    - Steps (planned/done/skipped) with timestamps
    - Summary stats and short narrative auto-generated (optional)
- The user can download/share it, but no in-app sharing.

DATA MODEL (Prisma)
- User(id, email unique, passwordHash, locale, createdAt)
- Objective(id, userId, title, description, constraintsJson, privateMode boolean, status active|archived, createdAt, updatedAt)
- StepSuggestion(
    id, objectiveId, createdAt,
    model, promptHash,
    stepJson (JSON),
    fingerprint (string),
    status proposed|planned|done|skipped,
    skipReason nullable,
    userFeedback nullable
  )
- Guest storage:
  - If guest mode: store objectives + steps in local storage/IndexedDB with same schema shape.
  - Provide a "Convert Guest to Account" flow that migrates local data into the DB after signup.

DUPLICATE PREVENTION
- Store a deterministic fingerprint per step, derived from:
  action_type + main_entity + outcome_type
- Block re-suggestions by fingerprint per objective.
- Also do near-duplicate blocking:
  - normalize strings (lowercase, remove punctuation/stopwords)
  - compute similarity and block if too close
- If user clicks "Regenerate", it must avoid blocked_fingerprints and blocked_examples.

LLM GENERATION CONTRACT
- ALWAYS return strict JSON.
- If the objective is too vague, ask exactly ONE clarifying question instead of generating a step:
  Return JSON: { "needs_clarification": true, "question": "..." }
- Otherwise return:
  {
    "needs_clarification": false,
    "step_title": "...",
    "expected_outcome": "...",
    "prerequisites": ["..."],
    "estimated_minutes": 10|20|30|45|60,
    "dependency": "none"|"needs-approval"|"waiting-on-someone",
    "template": { "type": "email"|"message"|"checklist", "content": "..." } | null,
    "fingerprint_parts": { "action_type": "...", "main_entity": "...", "outcome_type": "..." }
  }
- Enforce with zod schema validation. If invalid, retry once with a repair prompt; if still invalid, show a user-friendly error.

PRIVACY / SAFETY
- Do not log objective text or step content to console in production.
- privateMode per objective:
  - If enabled: send only title + a redacted summary to the LLM (no description/constraints), and warn the user in UI.
- Rate limit generation per user (e.g., 30/day) and per objective (e.g., 10/hour).
- Store minimal telemetry (counts only), no raw content.

